{"term":"jury","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:7f9c20f960fd5d25b2","definition":"A group of individuals chosen from the general population to hear and decide a case in a court of law.","example":"And so the jury and he approached, as if this were a time of peace instead of one of the greatest world disturbances ever known in history, the question whether the prosecution had proved to the jury’s satisfaction that George Joseph Smith was guilty of murder. The jury were the shield which stood between him and death, unless, to the jury’s satisfaction, he was proved to be guilty. Yet while they were the shield of the man accused, they were also the Sword of the State; and if the man were proved guilty, they were the servants of the State to punish him. Their respective functions were these: he the judge, had to settle the law, and the jury must take the law from him. The jury were judges of fact.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antijury","be judge and jury","grand jury","hung jury","judge, jury and executioner","jury box","jury duty","jury equity","jury is out","juryless","juryman","jury mast","jury nullification","jury of half-tongue","jury of matrons","jury panel","juryperson","jury pool","jury rig","jury-rigged","jury rigging","jury service","jury tampering","jury trial","jurywoman","nonjury","party jury","petit jury","petty jury","police jury"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jury#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b7765ed5d984412384","definition":"A group of judges in a competition.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antijury","be judge and jury","grand jury","hung jury","judge, jury and executioner","jury box","jury duty","jury equity","jury is out","juryless","juryman","jury mast","jury nullification","jury of h